###############################################################################
# AUC — auction lifecycle (Dev 4)
# The whole file can be run top to bottom (request 1 passes its id to the requests after it)
#
# Covered so far: AUC-001 create a private draft, AUC-002 pre-publish validation,
# AUC-003 hidden reserve, AUC-004 preview + publish, AUC-005 buyer visibility, AUC-006 edit/cancel, AUC-007 auction end, AUC-008 Hot Auctions + browse sections
###############################################################################

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@admin   = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@sellerA = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
@buyer   = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004
@catCollectibles = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000103

# AUTH-008 — MockAuthGuard has been removed; every request needs a real bearer token
# Run `pnpm --filter api exec prisma db seed`, then copy the @xToken lines it prints
# and paste them here (tokens expire per JWT_ACCESS_TTL — once you start getting 401, seed again)
@adminToken   =
@sellerAToken =
@buyerToken   =

#=============================================================================
# 1. Create a draft (AUC-001)
#=============================================================================

### AUC-001 create — a draft with every field filled in. expect 201 + status DRAFT
# reservePrice must come back too, because the caller is the "draft owner" (AUC-003)
# originalEndAt and currentEndAt must both equal the scheduledEndAt that was sent
# @name createDraft
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Vintage Seiko 5 Automatic",
  "description": "Created from 08-auction.http — cleaned last year, original factory strap",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "USED",
  "startingPrice": 3000,
  "minBidIncrement": 100,
  "reservePrice": 4500,
  "scheduledStartAt": "2026-09-01T10:00:00.000Z",
  "scheduledEndAt": "2026-09-01T12:00:00.000Z",
  "imageUrls": [
    "https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Seiko+Front",
    "https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Seiko+Back"
  ]
}

@draftId = {{createDraft.response.body.$.id}}

### AUC-001 create — an incomplete draft (no reserve/schedule/images). expect 201
# Meant to pass: the SRS puts the completeness check in AUC-002, "before publishing",
# not when saving a draft — the response must have reservePrice: null, images: []
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Unfinished draft",
  "description": "No images or schedule yet",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "startingPrice": 500,
  "minBidIncrement": 50
}

#=============================================================================
# 2. Drafts are private (AUC-001)
#=============================================================================

### AUC-001 detail — the owner opens their own draft. expect 200 + sees reservePrice
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{draftId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-001 detail — another user opens the same draft. expect 404
# Must be 404, not 403 — the answer must not confirm that the draft exists
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{draftId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### AUC-001 detail — not logged in. expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{draftId}}

### AUC-001 list — the owner sees all their own drafts. expect 200 + items ≥ 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-001 list — anyone else sees an empty list. expect 200 + items: []
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

#=============================================================================
# 3. Cases that must fail (no 500s allowed)
#=============================================================================

### permissions — an admin can't create an auction (SRS §2: admins oversee, they don't sell). expect 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Admin should not be able to create this",
  "description": "Must be rejected by RolesGuard",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "startingPrice": 100,
  "minBidIncrement": 10
}

### permissions — no Authorization header. expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Not logged in",
  "description": "Must be rejected by AccessTokenGuard",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "startingPrice": 100,
  "minBidIncrement": 10
}

### category — an id that doesn't exist. expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Nonexistent category",
  "description": "Must get Category not found",
  "categoryId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000009999",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "startingPrice": 100,
  "minBidIncrement": 10
}

### category — a deactivated category (ADR-0001). expect 400
# Can't be hit directly yet: Dev 2's ADM-003 is still NotImplemented
# Workaround for now — open `pnpm --dir apps/api exec prisma studio` and set
# categories.is_active = false for {{catCollectibles}} before sending this block, then set it back
# (an automated test already covers this case in test/auction.e2e-spec.ts)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Deactivated category",
  "description": "Must get Category is not active",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "startingPrice": 100,
  "minBidIncrement": 10
}

### validation — starting price must be > 0. expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Starting price of zero",
  "description": "Must be rejected by @IsPositive",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "startingPrice": 0,
  "minBidIncrement": 10
}

### validation — title is only whitespace (empty after Trim). expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "   ",
  "description": "Must be rejected by @Trim + @IsNotEmpty",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "startingPrice": 100,
  "minBidIncrement": 10
}

### validation — sneaking in a field that is not in the DTO. expect 400
# The client must never set status itself — a draft is always created as DRAFT
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Sneakily setting status",
  "description": "Must be rejected by forbidNonWhitelisted",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "startingPrice": 100,
  "minBidIncrement": 10,
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### validation — a draft id that is not a UUID. expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/not-a-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

#=============================================================================
# 4. Pre-publish validation (AUC-002)
#=============================================================================
# A read-only checklist — doesn't change the draft's status
# ready: true  = passes every criterion, ready for AUC-004 publish
# ready: false = issues[] says what's left (field = the form field name, not the column name)

### AUC-002 — the complete draft from request 1. expect 200 + ready: true, issues: []
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{draftId}}/validation
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-002 — a draft with no schedule or images yet. expect 200 + ready: false
# issues must contain all 3 of START_AT_REQUIRED, END_AT_REQUIRED, IMAGES_REQUIRED
# @name draftIncomplete
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Unfinished draft",
  "description": "No images or schedule yet",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "startingPrice": 500,
  "minBidIncrement": 50
}

@incompleteId = {{draftIncomplete.response.body.$.id}}

### AUC-002 — the unfinished draft's checklist. expect ready: false + 3 issues
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{incompleteId}}/validation
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-002 — end time before start time. expect ready: false + END_AT_NOT_AFTER_START_AT
# @name draftBadSchedule
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Times swapped",
  "description": "End time is before start time",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "startingPrice": 500,
  "minBidIncrement": 50,
  "scheduledStartAt": "2026-09-01T12:00:00.000Z",
  "scheduledEndAt": "2026-09-01T10:00:00.000Z",
  "imageUrls": ["https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Only"]
}

@badScheduleId = {{draftBadSchedule.response.body.$.id}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{badScheduleId}}/validation
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-002 — reserve below the starting price. expect ready: false + RESERVE_BELOW_STARTING_PRICE
# @name draftLowReserve
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Reserve below the starting price",
  "description": "3000 vs 2999",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "NEW",
  "startingPrice": 3000,
  "minBidIncrement": 100,
  "reservePrice": 2999,
  "scheduledStartAt": "2026-09-01T10:00:00.000Z",
  "scheduledEndAt": "2026-09-01T12:00:00.000Z",
  "imageUrls": ["https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Only"]
}

@lowReserveId = {{draftLowReserve.response.body.$.id}}

###
# The response must never show the number 2999 — it may only say "breaks the rule" (AUC-003)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{lowReserveId}}/validation
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-002 — someone else asks for another user's draft checklist. expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{draftId}}/validation
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### AUC-002 — not logged in. expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{draftId}}/validation

### AUC-002 — a draft id that is not a UUID. expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/not-a-uuid/validation
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

#=============================================================================
# 5. Preview and Publish (AUC-004)
#=============================================================================
# preview = read-only, no status change / publish = actually changes the status
# Target status rule: start time not reached yet -> SCHEDULED, already reached -> ACTIVE
#
# ⚠️ Dates in this file are fixed around 2026-09-01; if the real date is past them
#    you will get END_AT_IN_THE_PAST — change them to future dates before sending

### AUC-004 preview — the owner sees what buyers will see. expect 200
# The result must never contain reservePrice, only reserveMet (AUC-003)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{draftId}}/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-004 preview — send again and check the draft is still DRAFT. expect status: DRAFT
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{draftId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-004 preview — someone else asks for the preview. expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{draftId}}/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### AUC-004 publish — an incomplete draft (no images/schedule). expect 400 + issues[]
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{incompleteId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-004 publish — a complete draft whose start time has not arrived. expect 200 + SCHEDULED
# publishedAt must be set, startedAt must be null
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{draftId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-004 publish — publish the same one again. expect 404
# It is no longer a DRAFT, so it isn't found — prevents double-publishing without relying on the client
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{draftId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-004 publish — a draft whose start time has arrived. expect 200 + ACTIVE
# @name draftStartsNow
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Auction starts immediately",
  "description": "Start time is in the past, end time has not arrived yet",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "USED",
  "startingPrice": 1000,
  "minBidIncrement": 50,
  "scheduledStartAt": "2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "scheduledEndAt": "2026-12-31T00:00:00.000Z",
  "imageUrls": ["https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Live"]
}

@startsNowId = {{draftStartsNow.response.body.$.id}}

###
# startedAt must be set too, not just publishedAt
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{startsNowId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-004 publish — end time has already passed. expect 400 + END_AT_IN_THE_PAST
# @name draftExpired
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Already expired",
  "description": "Both start and end times are in the past",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "USED",
  "startingPrice": 1000,
  "minBidIncrement": 50,
  "scheduledStartAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "scheduledEndAt": "2026-01-02T00:00:00.000Z",
  "imageUrls": ["https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Expired"]
}

@expiredId = {{draftExpired.response.body.$.id}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{expiredId}}/validation
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{expiredId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-004 publish — someone else publishes our draft. expect 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{startsNowId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### AUC-004 publish — not logged in. expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{startsNowId}}/publish

#=============================================================================
# 6. Buyer visibility (AUC-005)
#=============================================================================
# Published = public immediately, from SCHEDULED on — no need to wait for ACTIVE
# but biddingOpen is true only once it enters ACTIVE
#
# This route is @Public — it works without a token
# If a token is sent and the caller is the owner, reservePrice is included as well

### AUC-005 — a logged-out visitor views a published auction. expect 200
# Must not include reservePrice, only reserveMet + biddingOpen
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{draftId}}

### AUC-005 — another logged-in user views it. expect 200 + still no reservePrice
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{draftId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### AUC-005 — the owner views their own auction after publishing. expect 200 + sees reservePrice
# After publishing, /auctions/drafts/:id no longer finds it (it isn't a DRAFT anymore)
# so this is the only way a seller can still see their own reserve
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{draftId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-005 — an auction that is already ACTIVE. expect 200 + biddingOpen: true
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{startsNowId}}

### AUC-005 — an unpublished draft. expect 404
# Must be 404 even when the owner calls it — this route doesn't serve DRAFTs
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{incompleteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-005 — an id that doesn't exist. expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000099ff

### AUC-005 — an id that is not a UUID. expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/not-a-uuid

### AUC-005 — check that :id doesn't swallow the `drafts` path. expect 401 (not 400/404)
# If @Get(':id') were accidentally placed above the drafts routes, this case would break
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts

#=============================================================================
# 7. Edit / cancel (AUC-006)
#=============================================================================
# Editing and cancelling are only allowed while DRAFT or SCHEDULED, and with no bids yet
# Once ACTIVE, the core data can't be touched — cancelling while ACTIVE is an admin job (ADM-001)
#
# Editing a SCHEDULED auction re-runs the AUC-002 validation
# because a published auction must never become incomplete

### AUC-006 — create a draft to try editing/cancelling
# @name draftToEdit
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Edit test item",
  "description": "Will be edited and then cancelled in the next blocks",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "USED",
  "startingPrice": 3000,
  "minBidIncrement": 100,
  "reservePrice": 4500,
  "scheduledStartAt": "2026-09-01T10:00:00.000Z",
  "scheduledEndAt": "2026-09-01T12:00:00.000Z",
  "imageUrls": ["https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Before"]
}

@editId = {{draftToEdit.response.body.$.id}}

### AUC-006 — edit title and description while DRAFT. expect 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{editId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "New title after editing",
  "description": "New description"
}

### AUC-006 — sending new imageUrls = replaces the whole set, not appended. expect 200 + images has 1 image
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{editId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "imageUrls": ["https://placehold.co/600x400?text=After"]
}

### AUC-006 — a DRAFT can be edited into an incomplete state (remove all images). expect 200
# The draft isn't published yet, so it doesn't have to pass AUC-002
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{editId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "imageUrls": []
}

### AUC-006 — sneaking in a field that is not in the DTO. expect 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{editId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### AUC-006 — someone else edits our auction. expect 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{editId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Not mine but editing anyway"
}

### AUC-006 — not logged in. expect 401
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{editId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Not logged in"
}

### AUC-006 — editing an auction that is already ACTIVE. expect 400
# {{startsNowId}} was already published as ACTIVE in block 5
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{startsNowId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Too late, cannot edit"
}

### AUC-006 — cancelling an ACTIVE auction. expect 400
# While ACTIVE, only an admin may handle it (ADM-001)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{startsNowId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Seller cannot cancel while ACTIVE"
}

### AUC-006 — cancel a draft with a reason. expect 200 + status CANCELLED
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{editId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Item has a defect, withdrawing it for now"
}

### AUC-006 — cancelling the same one again. expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{editId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### AUC-006 — editing an auction that was already cancelled. expect 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{editId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Already cancelled, cannot edit"
}

### AUC-006 — cancel without a reason. expect 200
# The seller is not forced to give a reason (unlike ADM-001, where an admin must always record one)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{incompleteId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

#=============================================================================
# 8. Ending the auction (AUC-007)
#=============================================================================
# Outcome: highest bid that meets the reserve -> SOLD + record the winner/winning price
#          no bids at all, or reserve not met -> UNSOLD
#
# ⚠️ There is no scheduler yet, so an auction ends when "someone reads" an expired auction
#    (GET /auctions/:id) — however many times it is called, it ends once, with a single ENDED event
#
# ⚠️ There is no bidding endpoint yet (BID-001), so manual testing has to insert bids through Prisma Studio
#    or SQL first, then send the GET — an automated test fully covers this in auction.e2e-spec.ts

### AUC-007 — prepare an expired auction (after sending, edit current_end_at yourself)
# @name auctionToEnd
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Auction about to end",
  "description": "Used to test SOLD/UNSOLD outcomes",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "USED",
  "startingPrice": 3000,
  "minBidIncrement": 100,
  "reservePrice": 4500,
  "scheduledStartAt": "2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "scheduledEndAt": "2026-12-31T00:00:00.000Z",
  "imageUrls": ["https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Ending"]
}

@endingId = {{auctionToEnd.response.body.$.id}}

### publish it to ACTIVE first. expect 200 + ACTIVE
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{endingId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

###
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Before sending the next block, open prisma studio and do 2 things to this auction:
#   1. set current_end_at to a time in the past
#   2. (for SOLD) add a row in bids: auction_id = {{endingId}},
#      bidder_id = {{buyer}}, amount = 5000, sequence_no = 1,
#      client_request_id = any uuid
#      - use amount 4499 instead to get UNSOLD (below the 4500 reserve)
#      - no bids at all also gives UNSOLD
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### AUC-007 — reading an expired auction = ends it. expect 200 + SOLD or UNSOLD
# The response must not show reservePrice even though the reserve decides the outcome (AUC-003)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{endingId}}

### AUC-007 — send again. expect the same result, unchanged
# Check in prisma studio: auction_events must have exactly one ENDED row
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{endingId}}

### AUC-007 — the owner views the result. expect 200 + can see reservePrice (owner only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{endingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### AUC-007 — an auction that has not expired must not be ended. expect 200 + ACTIVE
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{startsNowId}}

#=============================================================================
# 9. Hot Auctions (AUC-008)
#=============================================================================
# A public list of running auctions, ordered by a fixed 3-level rule:
#   1. number of accepted bids, most -> fewest
#   2. current end time, soonest -> latest
#   3. auction id
#
# There is no `sort` query to change the order — the SRS forbids special flags or hidden scoring
# Only ACTIVE is shown (SCHEDULED / CANCELLED / ended / removed are not in the list)

### AUC-008 — a logged-out visitor views hot auctions. expect 200 + items[] + meta
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions

### AUC-008 — 5 items at a time. expect 200 + at most 5 items
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?limit=5

### AUC-008 — page 2. expect 200 + no overlap with page 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?page=2&limit=5

### AUC-008 — check reservePrice doesn't appear anywhere in the list (AUC-003)
# Go through every item: none may have a reservePrice key
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?limit=100

### AUC-008 — limit above the cap of 100. expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?limit=500

### AUC-008 — page is 0. expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?page=0

### AUC-008 — page is not a number. expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?page=abc

### AUC-008 — sending sort anyway. expect 400
# The client must not change the order — the DTO has no such field, so forbidNonWhitelisted rejects it
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?sort=price_asc

#=============================================================================
# 10. Browse sections (extending AUC-008)
#=============================================================================
# The home page has 4 cards: hot / ending soon / starting soon / recently ended
# All four use the same endpoint, differing only in `section`
#
# Only `hot` is in the SRS; the other three come from the home page design
#
# Important: the client can only pick a "section name" — it cannot change the order itself
# Each section has a fixed where + orderBy on the server, so it doesn't conflict with AUC-008's rule
# against special flags or hidden scoring
#
# Every section shows only statuses buyers can already see (AUC-005)
# DRAFT / CANCELLED / removed never appear in any section

### section — sending nothing = exactly the same hot list as before. expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions

### section — sending hot explicitly must match the above. expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?section=hot

### section — ending soon: ACTIVE ordered by currentEndAt soonest -> latest. expect 200
# Uses currentEndAt, not originalEndAt — an auction that got extended (BID-004)
# moves down the list instead of staying at the top as if it's about to close
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?section=ending-soon

### section — starting soon: SCHEDULED ordered by scheduledStartAt. expect 200
# Not open for bidding yet, but buyers can look ahead (AUC-005)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?section=starting-soon

### section — recently ended: SOLD + UNSOLD ordered by endedAt newest -> oldest. expect 200
# Uses endedAt (when it actually settled, AUC-007), not currentEndAt, which is only when it "should end"
# CANCELLED isn't in this list, because it isn't a public status
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?section=recently-ended

### section — pagination within a section works as normal. expect 200 + that section's meta.total
# meta.total must count only the section, not the whole table
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?section=starting-soon&limit=4

### section — the 4 home page cards, one call each like this (4 items per card)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?section=hot&limit=4

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?section=ending-soon&limit=4

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?section=starting-soon&limit=4

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?section=recently-ended&limit=4

### section — a section name that doesn't exist. expect 400
# No silent fallback to hot — a screen asking for the wrong section is a screen with a bug
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?section=most-expensive

### section — misspelled. expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?section=ending_soon

### section — sending status anyway. expect 400
# The DTO has no such field, so forbidNonWhitelisted rejects it
# Only a section name can be chosen; filters cannot be composed by hand
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions?status=SOLD
